; [CHOSEN, not recovered] - input to `lib /def:` so this image can IMPORT from the shipped
; Memory.dll rather than resolve it at run time. Only the three names both shipped images import
; are listed; `dumpbin /exports Memory.dll` shows 32.
;
; The decorated names are copied verbatim from `dumpbin /imports RendDX9.dll`. Modern MSVC mangles
; the declarations in Code/RendDX9Abi/BfMemory.h to these same three strings, which is what makes a
; plain C++ declaration enough to bind against a 2009 DLL.
LIBRARY Memory
EXPORTS
    ?addMemoryName@memory@hfe@dice@@YAHPBD@Z
    ?bf_malloc@memory@hfe@dice@@YAPAXIH@Z
    ?bf_free@memory@hfe@dice@@YAXPAX@Z
